WEBVTT

00:04.400 --> 00:06.110
You're so weak.

00:06.480 --> 00:08.610
Not even worth leaving alive.

00:10.830 --> 00:13.240
It really is humorous.

00:13.240 --> 00:17.740
You expected to slay the 
paper umbrella like this?

00:29.880 --> 00:37.640
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

01:51.000 --> 01:56.010
<b>Efflorescence</b>

01:58.300 --> 02:00.300
You know of the paper umbrella?

02:00.300 --> 02:05.180
I know you aspire to kill it 
to avenge your slain family.

02:05.180 --> 02:07.430
Do you know where it is?!

02:07.430 --> 02:11.180
And you've been training 
in order to take your revenge.

02:11.980 --> 02:14.120
But if this is as far as it's gotten you,

02:14.120 --> 02:18.240
your resentment must run shallow after all!

02:22.070 --> 02:23.080
Tell me!

02:43.920 --> 02:45.280
Harder!

02:45.280 --> 02:46.220
Harder!

02:46.220 --> 02:48.230
Try harder!

02:50.220 --> 02:51.350
Hyoma!

02:59.210 --> 03:00.400
Welcome!

03:00.400 --> 03:01.910
Kai!

03:08.000 --> 03:10.190
Now it's getting fun!

03:10.190 --> 03:12.330
Are you up next, Nagi?!

03:12.950 --> 03:14.520
Don't be stupid.

03:14.520 --> 03:17.630
I know I can't take you in a one-on-one...

03:17.630 --> 03:20.880
But the kid told me everything!

03:21.570 --> 03:22.640
Itsuki?!

03:23.190 --> 03:23.880
I...

03:24.330 --> 03:26.800
I'm sorry, Kai-sama.

03:26.800 --> 03:27.640
We're out of time.

03:27.640 --> 03:29.770
W-Wait...

03:33.060 --> 03:35.300
I told you to hide...

03:36.180 --> 03:38.780
Because you're so extremely weak.

03:40.680 --> 03:43.780
Damn it, what a pain-in-the-ass old bastard.

03:44.140 --> 03:45.160
Nagi.

03:45.720 --> 03:47.980
Tell me what's going on here.

03:47.980 --> 03:49.540
Or rather... first...

03:50.040 --> 03:52.040
Could you get me down from here?

03:54.840 --> 03:56.700
Oh, no way!

03:56.700 --> 03:57.590
What, really?

03:57.590 --> 04:01.660
There's gotta be some hot guys 
who like the Hyakunin Isshu!

04:01.660 --> 04:04.700
Who cares if they like the Hyakunin Isshu?

04:04.700 --> 04:05.720
As long as they're hot.

04:05.720 --> 04:07.790
What are we talking about?

04:07.790 --> 04:11.180
They're plotting to rope in good-looking 
guys from the new students.

04:11.180 --> 04:13.230
Ah. Right.

04:13.230 --> 04:15.710
Huh?! Botan-senpai's put off?!

04:15.710 --> 04:16.460
Why?

04:16.460 --> 04:19.480
You know our slogan this year is, 
"Pick up some male club members!"

04:19.480 --> 04:20.680
Now, now.

04:20.680 --> 04:22.490
Calm down, my dear girls.

04:23.110 --> 04:25.920
This is what they call "the leisure 
of the romantically attached."

04:24.490 --> 04:26.490
<b>Romantically attached</b>

04:26.780 --> 04:29.550
I knew it! Kunato-san is her boyfriend!

04:29.550 --> 04:30.570
Huh?!

04:30.570 --> 04:32.120
Don't look down on us!

04:32.880 --> 04:34.180
Look...

04:35.120 --> 04:37.290
Can you guys just tidy up already?

04:41.740 --> 04:45.380
Dating... Romance...

04:48.440 --> 04:50.390
Loving someone.

04:53.160 --> 04:57.150
All terrifying things... and 
they make them look so easy.

05:00.230 --> 05:01.370
A greeting?

05:01.780 --> 05:05.720
I've heard rumors here and 
there of your existence.

05:05.720 --> 05:08.280
I got permission to see you myself.

05:08.280 --> 05:11.410
And you went too damn far as always!

05:11.410 --> 05:13.440
I have to amuse myself somehow.

05:13.440 --> 05:18.290
Besides, you had a little fun 
with Itsuki yourselves.

05:18.290 --> 05:21.170
That wasn't exactly fun!

05:22.070 --> 05:24.470
How was I supposed to know 
she was that damn weak?

05:24.470 --> 05:27.470
Well, they said they were 
gonna try to stop you,

05:27.470 --> 05:29.510
so I figured I'd try...

05:30.600 --> 05:31.970
Wait a minute.

05:33.190 --> 05:35.730
What do you know about the paper umbrella?

05:36.270 --> 05:41.440
That's the question you attempted 
to force me to answer, yes?

05:41.440 --> 05:47.110
I therefore determine that you are not yet 
strong enough to warrant an answer.

05:47.750 --> 05:48.890
Am I wrong?

05:49.790 --> 05:52.030
That's my estimation.

05:52.030 --> 05:56.380
I met Kunato Hayato and Kusui before,

05:56.380 --> 05:59.070
and you are far weaker even than they,

05:59.070 --> 06:01.500
who were slain by the 
paper umbrella at the time.

06:01.500 --> 06:04.760
Why don't you even use your own weapon?

06:05.800 --> 06:09.830
Is using the ones you received 
from them a way to remember them?

06:10.510 --> 06:12.520
A ridiculous obsession.

06:14.050 --> 06:18.060
You can give it a rest now, Kai.

06:18.510 --> 06:19.940
You think I'm being cruel?

06:19.940 --> 06:23.070
You're far worse than I am, Nagatsuki.

06:24.480 --> 06:26.070
What do you mean by that?

06:26.070 --> 06:30.580
Placing Kunato Hyoma with Nagatsuki Botan...

06:31.120 --> 06:34.200
That's a true act of cruelty.

06:35.650 --> 06:38.280
What should we do for the after-party?

06:42.800 --> 06:43.960
Hyoma-san?

06:44.410 --> 06:46.210
And... who?

06:46.980 --> 06:51.720
As long as the boy remains near her, 
he'll attempt to protect her.

06:52.060 --> 06:54.220
He'll consider it his duty.

06:54.720 --> 06:58.230
What could be more ironic, then?

06:58.920 --> 07:01.840
The paper umbrella who 
killed his brother and sister...

07:01.840 --> 07:05.680
The one responsible for its activation

07:05.680 --> 07:08.440
was Nagatsuki Botan herself!

07:11.080 --> 07:18.370
And of course, she doesn't want 
anyone protecting her anyway.

07:18.370 --> 07:25.130
Nagatsuki Botan is incapable of trusting 
anyone enough to wish for that.

07:25.130 --> 07:26.720
Ironic, isn't it?

07:27.400 --> 07:28.510
Kai!

07:29.190 --> 07:35.140
We'd appreciate it if you'd stop insulting 
our mistress with your baseless hunches.

07:35.440 --> 07:36.890
We'll crush you.

07:38.940 --> 07:41.080
Here we go—

07:44.350 --> 07:46.020
I said you were out of time.

07:47.590 --> 07:50.530
Besides, you've taken 
your mischief a little too far.

07:50.940 --> 07:53.850
Allow me to apologize on Kai-sama's behalf.

07:54.270 --> 07:56.650
He seems rather satisfied.

07:57.050 --> 07:59.470
I'll get him back in holding for a while,

07:59.470 --> 08:00.540
so please forgive him.

08:00.540 --> 08:01.660
Hold it!

08:01.980 --> 08:04.670
Nagi, suck it up for now.

08:04.670 --> 08:11.080
But Kai-sama is right that 
your situation is off-kilter.

08:11.960 --> 08:16.580
And... someone might potentially 
take advantage of that.

08:18.460 --> 08:20.280
Never forget that.

08:22.560 --> 08:25.270
Excuse me, Nagi, Suzuri.

08:25.960 --> 08:30.070
Do you think I could have a little time off?

08:30.070 --> 08:33.100
Don't let Kai's bullshit get to y—

08:34.130 --> 08:35.310
All right.

08:35.310 --> 08:36.070
Hey!

08:36.520 --> 08:40.330
But don't overdo it. And see that you return.

08:41.490 --> 08:42.500
Thank you.

08:46.600 --> 08:50.680
He's definitely hung up on what Kai said.

08:50.680 --> 08:53.800
It's about his siblings, after all.

08:53.800 --> 08:56.760
We can't exactly expect 
him to just shake it off.

08:57.380 --> 08:59.390
And what Kai said...

09:00.480 --> 09:03.020
It's true that there are rumors about it.

09:03.440 --> 09:06.920
That Botan's behind the 
paper umbrella incident?

09:06.920 --> 09:10.020
But it's just one of a dozen theories.

09:10.430 --> 09:15.640
We're just Saenome proxies, so there's 
no way for us to learn the truth, but...

09:17.640 --> 09:20.620
It would be a lie to say we know nothing.

09:21.000 --> 09:24.520
We need to be as open with him as we can.

09:27.160 --> 09:29.100
It's been four days now...

09:29.100 --> 09:32.250
I wonder where Hyoma-san is right now.

09:36.300 --> 09:37.050
Darn it!

09:37.050 --> 09:39.680
This is all Kai's fault!

09:39.680 --> 09:42.180
He does enjoy stirring the pot.

09:42.570 --> 09:44.430
It's not very nice.

09:44.430 --> 09:47.930
Hyoma apparently said 
he'd be back eventually.

09:47.930 --> 09:50.190
I'm sure there's no need to worry.

09:50.680 --> 09:52.980
My greater concern lies

09:53.690 --> 09:56.980
with Botan's recent despondency.

09:57.570 --> 10:02.300
<i>I wonder what his expression 
was in that moment.</i>

10:03.750 --> 10:05.900
I can't purge it from my mind.

10:06.330 --> 10:10.580
<i>If it's possible I was the cause of that...</i>

10:11.460 --> 10:12.660
<i>Then I...</i>

10:18.590 --> 10:21.350
Papa! Visitor!

10:24.340 --> 10:27.900
<i>The human in whom dwells a marebito 
from the land of the dead,</i>

10:27.900 --> 10:30.260
<i>that which serves as a tsukumogami's soul...</i>

10:31.740 --> 10:33.880
<i>Nagatsuki Botan.</i>

10:33.880 --> 10:37.360
<i>What kind of monster have you grown into?</i>

10:38.010 --> 10:39.390
P-Pleasure to meet you!

10:39.390 --> 10:41.080
My name is Nagatsuki Botan!

10:41.080 --> 10:43.540
Thank you for always looking after fy mamily!

10:44.870 --> 10:47.620
...m-my family.

10:48.520 --> 10:50.170
Ah, right...

10:50.650 --> 10:53.250
Though this is actually our second meeting.

10:54.340 --> 10:57.460
The first was when you were 
just a little thing, of course.

10:58.000 --> 11:00.630
It's no wonder you don't remember that.

11:00.630 --> 11:02.410
Have a seat.

11:03.390 --> 11:06.490
Tsubaki told me why you've come.

11:06.930 --> 11:12.850
You want to know how you're connected 
to the paper umbrella incident, then?

11:13.960 --> 11:14.700
Yes.

11:18.840 --> 11:20.840
Thank you for your help.

11:20.840 --> 11:22.480
I'm sorry for dropping in so... er...

11:22.480 --> 11:23.470
It's nothing.

11:23.470 --> 11:25.620
Though it was a bit sudden, true.

11:25.950 --> 11:31.470
But either way, the paper 
umbrella is Hyoma-kun's problem.

11:31.470 --> 11:33.560
Why're you so curious about it?

11:34.000 --> 11:36.750
Er... well...

11:40.660 --> 11:44.190
Is this one of those 
"I bet he hates me now" things?

11:44.190 --> 11:47.480
Listen to you, like a maiden in love!

11:49.860 --> 11:53.030
Tsubaki, have I said something rude?

11:54.500 --> 11:56.250
I think you hit the nail on the head.

11:56.250 --> 11:57.390
No! N-No, no!

11:57.390 --> 11:58.300
It's not like that!

11:58.300 --> 11:59.360
Um...

11:59.740 --> 12:02.890
That... Kai-san person said those things,

12:02.890 --> 12:05.520
and then Hyoma-san ran off somewhere...

12:05.520 --> 12:10.370
Since I happened to overhear it, 
I can't help but be... worried...

12:12.280 --> 12:14.350
Hyoma-chan ran off somewhere?

12:14.350 --> 12:16.750
He's been training with us, 
as a matter of fact.

12:17.860 --> 12:19.120
Representative Kadomori!

12:19.120 --> 12:20.640
I've completed my Ten Vessels Sparring!

12:20.640 --> 12:21.340
Next!

12:21.690 --> 12:23.550
Hyoma-san?!

12:24.140 --> 12:26.220
Botan? What brings you here?

12:26.220 --> 12:28.940
Convenient timing there.

12:28.940 --> 12:32.350
He came to stay with us three days ago.

12:32.950 --> 12:34.230
Representative Kadomori!

12:34.620 --> 12:38.410
I recently encountered Kai 
of the Three Great Tsukumogami,

12:38.410 --> 12:41.650
sparred with him, and was found lacking!

12:41.650 --> 12:47.160
I therefore wish to undertake training 
with the Saenome Kyoto Branch.

12:47.160 --> 12:48.390
Is this acceptable?!

12:49.630 --> 12:50.730
Hyoma-kun.

12:50.730 --> 12:53.330
Head home for now and take tomorrow off.

12:53.330 --> 12:55.330
What? But I still—

12:55.330 --> 13:01.210
Actually, the Ten Vessels Sparring you just 
completed is our household's final training!

13:01.210 --> 13:02.090
Unthinkable!

13:02.090 --> 13:04.010
I want you gone.

13:04.420 --> 13:06.840
You're a nuisance to have in our house.

13:11.360 --> 13:14.300
Hyoma-san, you forgot your scarf.

13:15.090 --> 13:16.280
You have my thanks.

13:16.680 --> 13:18.230
There's a surprise.

13:19.200 --> 13:22.170
You're a bit fond of Hyoma-kun, aren't you?

13:22.170 --> 13:24.990
Wouldn't you rather have him staying over?

13:24.990 --> 13:29.960
Seems like frequent visits over a long 
time would offer more chances than

13:29.960 --> 13:31.870
him learning it all in a 
short time and then leaving.

13:31.870 --> 13:35.790
Wouldn't him staying over 
make it easier to go after him

13:35.790 --> 13:38.000
when Nagatsuki Botan's not around?

13:39.670 --> 13:41.130
Well...

13:41.130 --> 13:42.390
Maybe.

13:46.650 --> 13:48.810
You heard us talking there?!

13:48.810 --> 13:50.040
I'm afraid so.

13:50.840 --> 13:53.610
And you went to ask Kadomori the truth?

13:54.240 --> 13:55.520
That's quite bold.

13:55.880 --> 14:00.150
I mean... you just left 
without saying anything, so...

14:01.590 --> 14:05.150
I thought you might not want to stay 
in our house anymore because of that.

14:07.190 --> 14:09.280
Of course I was worried.

14:11.110 --> 14:12.280
I apologize.

14:13.260 --> 14:18.280
But it should matter a lot to you, right?

14:19.850 --> 14:20.890
Well...

14:23.710 --> 14:27.050
To be frank, I assumed 
that part was nonsense.

14:28.450 --> 14:33.930
The idea of you being responsible for 
the paper umbrella is transparently false.

14:34.460 --> 14:38.600
I learned only one thing: that I am too weak.

14:39.350 --> 14:41.680
Thus, I must train.

14:41.680 --> 14:44.980
The next time we meet, I will force out 
the truth about the paper umbrella.

14:46.670 --> 14:49.110
You're really amazing, Hyoma-san.

14:49.970 --> 14:53.670
When you set your eye on something, 
you never waver in going after it.

14:54.280 --> 14:55.700
W-Well...

14:55.700 --> 14:58.340
You trust that part of yourself.

15:00.660 --> 15:01.540
Botan?

15:02.710 --> 15:07.140
There's another truth that 
tsukumogami, Kai, revealed.

15:08.280 --> 15:11.690
I really can't trust others.

15:14.930 --> 15:17.560
May I ask what happened?

15:19.850 --> 15:20.980
The truth is...

15:21.530 --> 15:23.640
I was kidnapped once.

15:24.560 --> 15:25.960
When I was seven,

15:26.460 --> 15:30.760
a whole parade of different 
relatives offered to take me in.

15:31.760 --> 15:33.320
Botan...

15:33.320 --> 15:35.330
Would you be Botan, then?

15:35.690 --> 15:39.370
One was a man with kind eyes, 
a distant relative.

15:39.910 --> 15:42.700
Another was my father's younger sister.

15:42.700 --> 15:44.550
She had a sour expression.

15:45.520 --> 15:50.090
It had been a little over three years since 
I was allowed to venture off the grounds.

15:50.090 --> 15:54.780
But I'd already seen lots of humans and 
other tsukumogami set their sights on me,

15:54.780 --> 15:57.560
as a vessel housing a marebito.

15:58.130 --> 16:01.940
My household and I were all on our guard.

16:02.410 --> 16:03.500
But...

16:05.320 --> 16:08.040
Because they were my first 
blood relatives, I guess...

16:08.510 --> 16:10.310
I wanted them to care for me.

16:11.440 --> 16:13.720
I decided to trust their kindness.

16:14.840 --> 16:19.080
The one who kidnapped me was the woman.

16:20.150 --> 16:24.830
So she was someone you should 
have been on your guard around?

16:25.520 --> 16:27.750
No, not her.

16:30.580 --> 16:31.760
She...

16:32.930 --> 16:34.260
Satsuki-san...

16:34.910 --> 16:36.780
She was trying to save me.

16:41.800 --> 16:43.710
Damn you!

16:43.710 --> 16:46.020
You can't get ahead of me, Satsuki!

16:46.380 --> 16:47.680
Give it back, now!

16:47.680 --> 16:51.480
That thing belongs to me!

16:58.780 --> 17:00.330
Botan-chan,

17:00.860 --> 17:03.320
sorry to put you through 
that scary experience.

17:04.230 --> 17:08.180
Satsuki-san was the one 
I was always watching out for.

17:08.720 --> 17:12.300
But I should have been 
watching out for the man.

17:12.300 --> 17:14.120
Botan-chan.

17:14.120 --> 17:15.740
You are human.

17:16.400 --> 17:18.950
You're a human's... my brother's child.

17:19.880 --> 17:22.570
I'm sorry for what those 
tsukumogami might think,

17:22.570 --> 17:25.320
but I won't let anybody use you.

17:31.560 --> 17:33.720
Let's live together.

17:34.700 --> 17:37.320
You'll find happiness as a human.

17:37.780 --> 17:38.520
Okay?

17:48.840 --> 17:51.840
While my guys were out searching for me,

17:53.820 --> 17:57.780
I was living a quiet, 
peaceful life with Satsuki-san.

18:01.170 --> 18:04.970
I'd been taken from my parents 
right after I was born,

18:04.970 --> 18:09.370
but Satsuki-san was like the mother 
I'd always dreamed about.

18:12.420 --> 18:14.810
If I could have stayed with her,

18:14.810 --> 18:17.190
maybe she could have been my mother for real.

18:24.150 --> 18:28.710
But those peaceful days 
came to an abrupt end.

18:44.290 --> 18:46.270
Satsuki-san...

18:46.270 --> 18:49.990
Botan...chan...

18:50.900 --> 18:52.790
No worries.

18:53.290 --> 18:57.150
I'll put Botan here to good use.

18:58.200 --> 19:01.660
Botan...chan...

19:07.750 --> 19:11.420
I don't remember anything after that.

19:12.120 --> 19:15.220
The next thing I knew, it was all over.

19:17.810 --> 19:20.520
And ever since then,

19:21.840 --> 19:23.580
I've been afraid...

19:24.920 --> 19:26.900
of being betrayed by those I care about.

19:27.700 --> 19:30.180
Of seeing people die protecting me.

19:32.400 --> 19:38.400
I'm unspeakably afraid of trusting anyone.

19:38.820 --> 19:44.110
I've learned how to interact confidently 
with both humans and tsukumogami.

19:44.110 --> 19:47.590
But that's the absolute best I can do.

19:52.960 --> 19:55.960
I'm afraid to go any further.

19:56.320 --> 19:57.460
Any further?

19:58.880 --> 20:00.970
Like to have a best friend.

20:00.970 --> 20:06.260
The kind of relationship where you 
trust all you are to someone else...

20:07.860 --> 20:11.100
Let alone love another person.

20:11.390 --> 20:12.440
I just can't.

20:14.060 --> 20:16.730
And so the person you are...

20:17.120 --> 20:19.360
Always marching forward,

20:20.840 --> 20:22.870
never hesitating...

20:25.030 --> 20:27.240
It's truly amazing to me.

20:30.290 --> 20:32.040
This is getting a little depressing, huh?

20:32.870 --> 20:33.940
Let's go home.

20:37.860 --> 20:38.630
Botan.

20:40.440 --> 20:42.520
You might find me acceptable.

20:43.840 --> 20:46.880
Uh... in what way?

20:46.880 --> 20:48.390
Well, I mean...

20:49.140 --> 20:51.640
Perhaps you might trust me.

20:53.220 --> 20:54.150
Do you agree?

20:54.630 --> 20:57.150
Um... what?

20:57.560 --> 21:00.400
After all, I refuse to die 
until I achieve my life's goal,

21:00.400 --> 21:04.700
and I am undergoing training now 
to ensure that is possible!

21:04.700 --> 21:05.660
You know this, do you not?!

21:05.660 --> 21:07.280
Y-Yes...

21:07.280 --> 21:08.110
I might add,

21:08.110 --> 21:12.040
do you think me skilled enough at manipulation 
as to successfully deceive you?!

21:12.040 --> 21:15.160
N-No, you're very awkward, in fact!

21:15.480 --> 21:17.270
A-Awkward?

21:18.420 --> 21:20.480
True enough, I suppose.

21:20.480 --> 21:25.050
Regardless, I feel that you might 
find me acceptably trustworthy.

21:25.420 --> 21:26.810
Do you agree?

21:28.770 --> 21:30.580
Well... I...

21:31.000 --> 21:31.900
I just...

21:32.600 --> 21:33.740
I...

21:34.370 --> 21:35.060
Botan.

21:35.700 --> 21:36.970
This I swear.

21:36.970 --> 21:39.660
I will not betray you. I will not die.

21:40.010 --> 21:41.030
I...

21:42.090 --> 21:46.070
I'll always keep you safe.

21:52.830 --> 21:53.690
Whe...

21:54.320 --> 21:54.990
Whe?

21:54.990 --> 21:56.970
Where did "keep you safe" come from?!

21:56.970 --> 21:59.280
It... It was merely an expression of resolve!

21:59.280 --> 22:02.840
And aren't you oversimplifying 
things just a tad?!

22:04.370 --> 22:05.420
But...

22:05.830 --> 22:08.340
But can I... really...

22:08.960 --> 22:12.100
Can I really, really trust you?

22:12.380 --> 22:13.180
Indeed.

22:13.590 --> 22:14.790
Bring it on!

22:20.520 --> 22:21.340
What is it?

22:21.340 --> 22:22.630
I...

22:23.340 --> 22:26.150
I don't think I've ever seen you...

22:27.040 --> 22:28.740
really smile before.

22:29.670 --> 22:30.740
Eh?

22:30.740 --> 22:34.110
Surely, I am as capable of smiling as anyone!

22:34.110 --> 22:37.050
But still! I've never actually seen it!

22:37.050 --> 22:41.450
Yu's even said, "I suspect he even lacks 
facial muscles," and stuff like that!

22:41.450 --> 22:42.420
That's very rude!

22:44.310 --> 22:46.670
You look kind of like a kid when you smile.

22:47.040 --> 22:49.080
I know not of what you speak!

22:49.080 --> 22:50.170
Fare thee well!

22:53.840 --> 22:58.060
<i>What a surprise... 
to hear her talk of old times.</i>

22:58.720 --> 23:01.100
<i>I thought it would take 
a lot longer for that.</i>

23:01.520 --> 23:02.900
<i>It's very promising.</i>

23:03.940 --> 23:06.700
Hey! Let's walk home together!

23:07.880 --> 23:09.450
Darn it...
